# ===========================================================================
# AgentFloat frontend — frontend/.env
#
# Copy to `.env`. Every variable here MUST be prefixed VITE_ to reach the
# browser bundle. That prefix is also a warning: anything you put here is
# PUBLIC. Never put a private key or an app secret in this file.
#
# The agent key and the gateway signer key live in server/.env, which the
# browser never sees.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Privy (Google / email sign-in) ----------------------------------------
# Create a free app at https://dashboard.privy.io, then paste its App ID here.
#
# The App ID is a public client-side identifier — it is safe to ship. The app
# SECRET is not, and belongs nowhere in this repo.
#
# In the Privy dashboard:
#   * Enable login methods: Google and Email (and Wallet, if you want the
#     treasury operator to connect MetaMask through the same navbar).
#   * Embedded wallets: create on login for all users.
#   * DO NOT enable smart wallets or gas sponsorship. x402 authorizes with an
#     EIP-712 permit2 signature, which only an EOA can produce. Privy's gas
#     sponsorship delegates the wallet via EIP-7702, giving the address contract
#     code and forcing ERC-1271 signature mode that the x402 client does not use.
#
# Leave this empty and the app still runs in operator-wallet mode: the navbar
# shows "Privy not configured", and the faucet and per-user wallets stay off.
VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Gateway port, if you changed it in server/.env. Vite's proxy must match.
#VITE_GATEWAY_PORT=4022

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYING THE FRONTEND (Vercel)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these in the Vercel dashboard, not here: Vite INLINES import.meta.env at
# BUILD time, so a variable added after the build does nothing. Changing one
# means redeploying.
#
# VITE_GATEWAY_URL — where the gateway lives, e.g. the Render service URL.
#   Unset (local development) every API call is relative and the Vite dev server
#   proxies /api and /paid to 127.0.0.1:4022. Vercel serves a static bundle with
#   no proxy, so a deployed frontend needs one of:
#     • this variable — the browser calls the gateway's origin directly, and the
#       gateway's GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS must list your Vercel domain; or
#     • a platform rewrite of /api and /paid to the gateway (frontend/vercel.json
#       documents it). Same-origin, so no CORS — but vercel.json cannot read an
#       environment variable, so the gateway URL gets committed to the repo.
#   No trailing slash needed; one is stripped.
#VITE_GATEWAY_URL=https://agentfloat-gateway.onrender.com
#
# VITE_GATEWAY_ADMIN_TOKEN — see the warning in server/.env.example before
# setting this. Anything here ships inside the public JavaScript bundle.
#VITE_GATEWAY_ADMIN_TOKEN=
